+# Final seam review, epic hg-blw, integration branch super-auto/graph-state-inspection
+
+Invocation inv-b9c53a9d-0c9e-4100-99aa-2184b61f229c. Source: base bfeb8f3104dd3783d67a46570c9f272e935012b5, head 2dfa656c7f98715fe66ca53c253de19f369a857d. Both were verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`. `bind-review-source` exited 0 before this file was written, and the file did not exist before then. The caller checkout was at HEAD 2dfa656 with a clean `git status --short` at the start and at the end of the review. It was not switched, restored or edited.
+
+## Inputs and method
+
+- I read the sixteen cluster reviews of this invocation, clusters.json, `bd show hg-blw --json` and `bd list --parent hg-blw --all`.
+- The epic points at the approved design doc, docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-07-graph-state-inspection/2026-11-07-graph-state-inspection-design.md. Its `## Requirement baseline` section (B1-B8, human scope change S1) is the acceptance standard I used.
+- The review is static. It reads `git show 2dfa656:<path>` across the cluster seams. I made no worktree and no build. The cluster 5, 8 and 10 reviewers already ran the relevant test tiers at this head in review-owned worktrees, and they reported leak check 0.
+- Seams traced across clusters:
+  - the hook writer chain: bootstrap `hook_command`/`codex_hook_command` → cli `seat --hook-prompt --stdin-payload` → inspect `loaded::record`, built on bootstrap `fit_hook`/`cut_body_bytes`/`part_digest`;
+  - the reader chain: inspect `roster::build_inner` and `stack` → `loaded::clone_view` → store `HistoryWalker::last_touches`;
+  - the occupant id producers: transcripts `report_args` (Claude) and observe `sessions` with model `harness::CODEX` (Codex);
+  - `roster --live`: cli `roster::live` → daemon `roster_live::handle` → inspect `build_with_bindings`/`overlay`, with compose `LazyMap::inspect` as the threads-state producer;
+  - `ops`: cli `ops` → plan `ops.list`;
+  - `doctor`: daemon `harness_hook_checks` → bootstrap `owned_hook_current`.
+
+## Requirement baseline trace
+
+- B1 (which seats are active) is delivered. The path is `herdr-graph roster [<scope>] [--all] [--json]` → `cli::roster::run` (HEAD pinned once) → `inspect::roster::build` → `Inventory::load`. It shows lifecycle, availability, pane, occupant with native id and transcript, threads state, manager and reload_required for each clone. It is daemon-free. `--live` adds the agent kind and status (B8).
+- B2 (which files are loaded into context per seat) is delivered.
+  - Producer: `herdr-graph setup claude|codex` installs commands that carry `--stdin-payload` (setup_claude.rs:208-219). At SessionStart, `cli::seat::hook_prompt` prints first, then calls `loaded::record` with the same `RenderedInstructions` and `HookFit` it printed.
+  - Readers: `roster --json` `clones[].instructions.parts`/`omitted` and `instructions stack <seat>` (manifest, hook-cap simulation, per-clone record) both go through `loaded::clone_view`.
+  - The writer and the reader compute the delivered set with the same `delivered(r, fit_hook(r, HOOK_RENDER_CAP))`. That rules out disagreement about which parts were cut or omitted.
+  - The writer keys the record by the `Resolution::Bound` clone at the instance root found by `locate_instance`. The readers open it at `GitStore::root()` with the clone record's id. These agree for the CLI and for the daemon.
+  - The record's parts are shown whatever the status, including `unknown`. So B2 is delivered for Codex too.
+  - tests/inspect_loaded.rs runs the exact installed command strings end to end.
+- B3 (state activity and latest modifications at global, space and seat) is delivered.
+  - `herdr-graph log [<scope>] [--since] [--limit] [--by] [--all] [--json]` → `HistoryWalker` + `LogQuery`.
+  - Roster `last_change` uses the same `LogQuery::matches` with `Scope::Seat`, `all: false`, in one walker pass.
+  - The journal side goes through `ops --seat/--teamspace/--limit/--json`. The CLI resolves names to ids at a pinned HEAD and sends `seat`/`teamspace` ids. `plan::ops` parses exactly those keys and filters on `Requester.seat`/`Requester.teamspace`. Production fills both through `requester_for`.
+- B4 (all sessions by space, seat or clone, with timestamps, newest first) is delivered.
+  - `herdr-graph sessions [<scope> | clone <c>]` → `Inventory::load` (live and archive) → `inspect::sessions::build`.
+  - Rows are sorted by `started` descending with an ns-id tiebreak, carry `total` and `tombstones`, and fall back to the transcript record.
+- B5 (staleness is shown, not notified) is delivered for Claude.
+  - The Claude occupant's native id comes from `session.report`, whose `capture.native_session_id` is the payload `session_id` (transcripts/capture.rs `report_args`). The observer path stems the Claude transcript path, which is `<session_id>.jsonl`. Both producers therefore agree with the id the hook records, and the identity-then-content rule reaches `current` and `stale`. `hook_chain_reaches_current_once_the_occupant_lands` covers this.
+  - No notice and no commit is added.
+  - For Codex, the occupant id is the file stem of Herdr's `agent_session` path (observe/sessions.rs:36-46), while the payload `session_id` is a bare id. §2.3 accepts `unknown` for a form difference, but only with the `codex session id form differs` note. That note cannot fire for this form (cluster 5 Must fix, carried below). The row is delivered under the spec's own Codex limit, with that labelling defect.
+- B6 (log hides bookkeeping by default) is delivered. `--all` defaults to false into `LogQuery.all`, and roster `last_change` also passes `all: false`.
+- B7 (harness-native files: presence, size and mtime, content never read) is delivered.
+  - harness_files.rs uses only metadata and read_dir. `content_never_opened` passes on a mode-000 file.
+  - There is one labelling defect: `origin`/`env` for `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` when the cwd is under $HOME (cluster 5 Must fix, carried below).
+- B8 (`roster --live` in scope now) and S1 (unmanaged objects only enumerated) are delivered.
+  - `cli::roster::live` → `roster.live`, registered by the production `compose_with` → one `pin_head`, the same `build_with_bindings` builder, exactly one `snapshot()`, and `overlay` with `unmanaged_of` listing only ids and labels.
+  - Daemon down exits 5.
+  - Tier 3 runs against a private Herdr and passed in cluster 10's run.
+  - The §2.2 threads-degraded rule is not met when the threads service is unreachable (cluster 3 Must fix, carried below). That is a spec defect inside B8's delivered path, not an undelivered row.
+- No baseline row is undelivered. No human scope change row is needed to cover a gap.
