+## Findings
+
+- src/bootstrap/setup_claude.rs:208-213 with src/cli/seat.rs:201: the installed Claude hook begins with an unbounded `p=$(cat)` before the binary prints, so the binary's bounded stdin read never protects the production chain; this contradicts the design's Unchanged behavior and hg-blw.12's held-open acceptance, and the held-open test bypasses the installed command (carried from cluster 11, confirmed as a seam defect).
+- src/inspect/loaded.rs:229-236 against src/observe/sessions.rs:36-46: the Codex occupant id is a Herdr rollout-path stem and the hook records the bare payload id; the stem comparison cannot detect that form, so the required form-differs note never fires (carried from cluster 5).
+- src/daemon/roster_live.rs:64-82 against src/daemon/compose.rs LazyMap::inspect: threads unreachable leaves `seat_view_error` unset, so `roster --live` reports `live_unavailable: null` with empty or stale refusals (carried from cluster 3, re-verified).
+- src/inspect/harness_files.rs:217-248: the Claude ancestor walk registers `$HOME/.claude/CLAUDE.md` as `origin: ancestor` before the user-level add, so the user file loses `origin: user` and `env: inspector` in the default layout (carried from cluster 5).
+- src/daemon/roster_live.rs:51-52 against src/inspect/mod.rs `fail`: an integrity error during scope resolution exits 1 under `--live` and 6 daemon-free.
+
+## Verdict
+not ready (roster --live threads-degraded state, Codex form-differs note, harness-file user origin, and the unbounded hook stdin read vs the never-blocks guarantee remain open)
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- src/daemon/roster_live.rs:64-82 with src/daemon/compose.rs LazyMap::inspect: when the threads seat read fails for any reason other than Rejected/Unsupported (service down, Disconnected, transport, discovery), roster.live must return seat_refusals/seat_lost null and live_unavailable.threads naming the reason (spec §2.2); record the last read outcome in a slot the handler reads and add a test that drives a Disconnected read instead of writing seat_view_error directly (cluster 3).
+- src/inspect/harness_files.rs:217-248: with the cwd under $HOME and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR unset, `$HOME/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is reported as `origin: ancestor` without `env: inspector`; run the user-level adds before the ancestor walk or let a user-level add override origin and env, and add a test with a cwd under the user's home (cluster 5).
+- src/inspect/loaded.rs:229-236: the `codex session id form differs` note never fires for Herdr's rollout-path occupant stem (`rollout-<ts>-<uuid>`) against the bare payload `session_id`, leaving a silent `unknown` (spec §2.1/§2.3); detect that form difference for the note only, without treating the ids as a match, record the payload form hg-blw.12 was to record, and test with a rollout-path occupant (cluster 5).
+- Design §2.3 vs Unchanged behavior and hg-blw.12, with src/bootstrap/setup_claude.rs:208-213: the installed Claude hook's unbounded `p=$(cat)` runs before the prompt prints, so a held-open stdin blocks `/seat` until the 10 s hook timeout; either bound the payload read in the installed command (size and time) or explicitly drop the held-open guarantee in the design with its rationale, and test the installed command, not only the bare binary, with a held-open stdin (cluster 11, confirmed as a cross-cluster seam).
