+## Untested scope
+- No test runs the installed Claude `hook_command` chain (`p=$(cat); …`) with a held-open stdin; tests/inspect_loaded.rs exercises only the bare binary.
+- No test covers roster.live while the threads service is unreachable (Disconnected); the only threads-degraded test sets seat_view_error by hand.
+- No test uses a Codex occupant whose native id came from a Herdr rollout path with a bare-uuid payload id, at unit or integration level.
+- No test runs harness-file discovery with a cwd under the user's home.
+- No test covers an integrity StoreError during roster.live scope resolution and its exit code.
+- roster.live with a non-empty scope, `all: true`, or a loaded record present is not exercised at the handler level.
+- Tier-3 `roster --live` covers only the happy path: agent kind and status, refusals and lost contents, an earlier-server binding and the degraded herdr text line are not exercised against a real Herdr through the binary.
+- No binary-level test lists populated `sessions` or `log` results (ordering, `clone <c>` on a real clone, `--by`, bookkeeping hidden and `--all`); only src/inspect unit tests cover them.
+- No integration test drives a truncated injection end to end (`cut` part, `omitted` labels, a cap-boundary move turning the record stale).
+- No end-to-end test runs `ops --seat/--teamspace --json` against a live daemon with requester-attributed ops.
+- `instructions stack --clone <c>` has only clap-level tests; no test resolves a clone through the CLI, including a same-named clone in another seat.
+- `instructions stack` has no test where `HistoryWalker::last_touches` fails.
+- `read_stdin_payload` timeout path with the bare binary is covered, but `codex_trust_note` in setup has no test.
+- `owned_hook_current` and `harness_hook_checks` error paths (unreadable or malformed settings) have no test.
+- `fit_hook` with a cut part that delivers zero body bytes has no test.
+- Roster and stack instruction status for retired seats and clones under `--all` is not exercised.
+- Roster and log behavior when a historical commit's tree holds an unparseable record has no test.
+- No HistoryWalker test pins first-parent behavior on a merge commit, a trailer whose record is absent from the diff, or record selection in an undo-shaped commit.
+- Roster `last_change` and HistoryWalker cost near the 5000-commit cap is unmeasured (Sort::TOPOLOGICAL prepares the full chain).
+- This seam review ran no build or tests; pass status at 2dfa656 is taken from the cluster 5, 8 and 10 runs in review-owned worktrees.
+- run.md at head was not validated with scripts/report-status.
